# GPUMD nep.in template for magnetic NEP training (model_type=4)
# BCC Fe — 200 structures (120 collinear + 80 non-collinear)
# Adjust values as needed for your specific training run.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Place train.xyz (from batch_outcar_to_exyz.py) in this directory
#   2. Optionally place test.xyz (holdout set) alongside
#   3. Run: /path/to/gpumd/src/nep train.xyz [test.xyz]
#   4. Output: nep.txt (trained model), *.out files (RMSE tracking)

# --- System definition ---
type          1 Fe
model_type    4

# --- Radial/angular basis ---
cutoff        4.0 4.0
n_max         4 4
basis_size    8 8
l_max         4

# --- Neural network ---
neuron        30

# --- Loss weights ---
lambda_e      1.0
lambda_f      1.0
lambda_v      0.1
lambda_torque 1.0
# lambda_moment is auto-derived from moment:R:3 in train.xyz; not a nep.in keyword

# --- Optimizer (SNES) ---
population    50
generation    100000

# --- Training/test split ---
batch         2000
# If no separate test.xyz, GPUMD auto-splits train.xyz

# --- Physical regularization ---
# BCC Fe elastic constants (GPa): C11=243, C12=146, C44=116
# Bulk modulus B = (C11+2*C12)/3 ≈ 178 GPa
# Shear modulus G = C44 ≈ 116 GPa
